        <h1 style="padding-bottom: 30px; font-size: 2em; font-weight: bold;text-align:left;">Medical Camps</h1>
        <p>In developing countries, pop-up medical camps are crucial, particularly in the aftermath of disasters. These camps serve as vital hubs for delivering immediate healthcare to communities facing disruptions in their regular medical services. In these situations, accessing a health centre can be a significant struggle, with some located miles away. When natural disasters, such as earthquakes or floods, occur, these temporary facilities step in quickly to bridge the gap. They play a pivotal role in ensuring that people, who might otherwise face challenges reaching a distant health centre, receive timely medical attention. These pop-up camps offer a rapid response to health challenges, acting as a lifeline for communities during difficult times.</p>
        <img src="~/Content/projects/health-services/health-care-1.jpg" style="width:100%;" />
